t(46, 1305, """Whenever I turn my face east, west and to the middle of the earth .. and look right and left, I find visual posts about some invention to solve such-and-such a problem .. some invention to solve such-and-such a problem .. and another invention to solve such-and-such a problem .. The Arabs are present on the scene, no doubt, but their achievements are weak (in number), not in quality, and most of the achievements are Western! These facts must make us realise that integration among human beings is the basis for solving humanity's problems, and that conflict and clash do not serve a humanity exhausted for no less than 100 years, nor the project of an Ummah that lost its compass 1407 years ago. Many Muslims think the Muslims lost the compass 100 years ago, whereas the Prophet ﷺ specified that the compass is his compass alone, and no other compass. His first compass was in a time that ended in the year 41 AH, and after it the compass disappeared; so we have been in a wilderness for 1407 years. It is not a wilderness that lasted 100 years or 200 years or 500 years or 900 years; rather it has lasted 1407 years .. We have been cut off from the reality of Islam for 1407 years, and that is a very long time .. A span of time in which the Ummah was lost and floundered .. Did it preserve its monotheism? Yes, that is true. Did it preserve the pillars of Islam? Yes, that is true. Did it worship its Mighty Lord by the texts of the Book and what is authentic of the Sunnah? Yes, that is true. So its wilderness was not that it left the religion, nor was its wilderness that it disbelieved, Allah forbid; rather its wilderness was that it lost its spirit. And nations, when they lose their spirit, fade and vanish. This Ummah has been fading and vanishing for 1407 years, and the bottom it has reached today is the one it has been heading towards since the year 41 AH; it reached the bottom in 1407 years. That it is still breathing, even if it breathes on a ventilator of pure destiny in whose existence it has no merit, is a good thing; for an Ummah that has been falling and tumbling towards the bottom for 1407 years should, by reason and logic, have perished, vanished and ceased to exist. But its survival is in itself proof of the mercy of Allah the Mighty towards it. As an Ummah we are not merely lost and astray; rather we have left the order of history altogether and fallen from the ranks of civilisation, and the meanings of dignity have been erased from the souls of many of the Ummah's children. This Ummah has come to need only one thing: a unity that unites its efforts and with which it sets out to live in real dignity, real honour and real freedom among the nations. The day that happens to it, it will have set out in the reverse direction, from the bottom to the top, gone beyond the fall it lived through for 1407 years, and been freed from its gravity and its pull downwards. And this in itself occurs only through a divine intervention (not the sign of the Smoke), since this divine intervention will be the only way out for the Ummah. Whoever thinks there is another way out, like the Muslim Brotherhood, which still dreams of ruling the Ummah and still lives in a coma after having offered the Ummah political failure, stillborn thought and political naivety; everyone who still thinks well of the Islamic movements, and everyone who thinks well of the ISIS people and those who wrong …""")

t(47, 60, """… Islam, who disfigured the image of this religion in the world; everyone who is still imprisoned by these in the thousand prisons of his mind needs to re-examine his mind.

Summary: the intervention of heaven is coming, by the power of our Mighty Lord; no believing man or woman doubts that. All those who call for revolutions against the rulers understand nothing of what I say, and all those who call for strife and bloodshed inside the countries of the Islamic world do not grasp the scale of the fall that has lasted 1407 years and understand nothing of it. That is why they think that rising against the rulers is the solution. This, as I said, confirms their naivety, the decay of their thought, the deviation of their compass, and their failure to understand the scale of what happened over 1407 years! They understood nothing.""")

t(47, 2165, """To complete the explanation of the saying of our Mighty Lord: {As for those women whose defiance you fear, admonish them, leave them alone in their beds, and strike them. Then if they obey you, seek no way against them. Allah is Most High, Most Great}

O Muslims .. A Muslim woman (a wife) may be subjected to striking only by this Qur'anic text; anything beyond that is injustice and aggression. Then it becomes easy to classify any husband and to know who he is! Is he one of the followers of the Prophet ﷺ, or one of the followers of Satan?
Among husbands is he who strikes his wife merely because she is angry, merely because her face is sullen, merely because something does not please her, merely because she does a thing and carries it out unconvinced, because she refuses to carry out something that harms her, in which obedience is not obligatory, since there is to be no harm and no reciprocating harm, and for dozens of reasons for which the husband may not touch her with ill; it is not permissible for him …""")

t(48, 60, """… nor lawful for him to hurt her, whether by abuse, insult, humiliation or striking.

Those who do that, by Allah they are the wrongdoers .. they are the wrongdoers .. By Allah they are not followers of our Prophet Muhammad ﷺ .. By Allah they are not his followers""")

t(48, 575, """A young man's father forced him into a university course he does not like and cannot bear, so the young man took the money and enrolled in a different course. Is there anything against him? Answer: No .. Because the root of the change in the nature of human life and societies today is that a new custom has arisen that did not exist before, namely the father educating his children, the males especially. The matter is no longer optional; this is how the world has become. And so earning a living has come to require university education or vocational, trade education. Forcing the son into a course the father wants and the son hates and cannot bear is not the father's right, because the boy will fail. But if the son chooses a specialisation other than the one his father wants, he must bear the consequences, and his father is absolved of responsibility for his life, which will hold good or bad opportunities according to the specialisation the boy chose. But at least the boy studied something he loves, as long as the study will not lead him into places of deviation in work contrary to the Shariah in the future, such as specialising in acting, music or gynaecology; all these are specialisations forbidden to a man, and the father has the right to prevent him from studying them. But the discussion was about permissible specialisations.""")

t(48, 1385, """I ask my brothers and sisters to pay attention to this important post about married life
First: let us establish some very important ethical points in understanding the saying of our Mighty Lord, hallowed be His names:
{As for those women whose defiance you fear, admonish them, leave them alone in their beds, and strike them. Then if they obey you, seek no way against them. Allah is Most High, Most Great}
🔴 Painful striking may happen, because we are human, and it occurred from the Prophet ﷺ
Painful striking does not mean flogging, crushing the body, breaking bones, or committing the disasters and calamities that Muslim husbands commit. Its upper limit is what happened to the Mother of the Believers Aisha
🔴 Painful striking must never be a method in striking, because the Prophet ﷺ did not do it as a habit and method; it occurred from him only once
🔴 Non-painful striking is that which causes slight pain, not harmful pain; it is a matter of judgement
🔴 Striking in itself the Prophet ﷺ did not practise as a habit or a method, whether the painful kind or the non-painful

Summary: in the relationship between spouses, as we see in the practice of the Prophet ﷺ, the basic rule is never, ever striking. But it is not said of one who struck his wife that he is not a man, nor is he to be insulted and transgressed against by a woman who does not understand her religion!

Why it is not said of a man who struck his wife justly, not unjustly, in accordance with the meanings of striking set out above and with the conditions of the noble verse; why it is not said of him that he is not a man:
Because the Prophet ﷺ was the Seal of the Prophets and Messengers and the leader of the Ummah, and his rank and awe make a wife's transgression against him impossible. Yet despite his rank and standing, marital situations and incidents happened to him. So what about an accountant, a teacher, a doctor, an electronics technician, a bus driver, a restaurant cook and a rubbish collector?

If the Prophet ﷺ was compelled to use painful (severe) striking, not the siwak, he being the leader of the whole Ummah, its master, its chief, its Prophet and its Messenger, then what is the engineer, the doctor, the teacher, the rubbish collector""")

t(49, 60, """and the bus driver to do?

Second: if striking occurred in the time of the first generation, with the best women of the world around the Prophet ﷺ, chosen, noble wives and Mothers of the Believers, and yet from them (may Allah be pleased with them) came mistakes that not only angered the Prophet ﷺ but angered Allah Most High regarding two wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and the incident is known; then what about a great number of the women of the society of 1447 AH - 2025 CE?

Third and last: did the Prophet ﷺ die holding to his word on striking women and his command to strike them, or did he die upon the cancellation of the verse revealed about striking women?

Answer: the Prophet ﷺ died upon two fundamental matters that created the true balance in Muslim society:
First: he conveyed from his Lord the verse of striking women when they are defiant
Second: to curb the unruliness of men's hands and to keep the application of the verse within the lawful limits, he ﷺ said: "Fear Allah regarding women"
And he ﷺ said: "Treat women well, for they were created from a rib, and the most crooked part of the rib is its top; so treat women well"

Summary: striking is legislation from Allah Most High. Whoever slanders and mocks it has disbelieved, whoever rejects and refuses it has disbelieved, and whoever says of it "empty talk", like one of the women preachers, has disbelieved .. It has limits whose overstepping makes retribution due from the transgressing husband, and striking has Shariah rules, causes, circumstances and conditions; the matter is not a game.

The Prophet ﷺ died while the legislation of striking from the Lord of the heavens and the earth, hallowed be His names, stood in force, and while the commands of our Mighty Lord not to wrong woman, clear commands in His Book in plain verses, some concerning woman and some concerning the human being as a whole, stood in force. And the Prophet ﷺ died while his bequest to treat women well stood in force and firm; none disputes it but a wrongdoer or an ignorant person.""")

t(49, 1590, """Sisters asked about the saying of Allah Most High in His Mighty Book: {As for those women whose defiance you fear, admonish them, leave them alone in their beds, and strike them. Then if they obey you, seek no way against them. Allah is Most High, Most Great}.

The question was about the nature of striking, and what striking is permitted by the Shariah in application of this verse when things between the husband and his wife have reached this degree of a bad relationship.

First, we affirm and believe that striking is part of the law of Allah Most High, whether a man applies it to his wife or not. If he does not apply it, out of forbearance on his part, he is not rejecting the Book of Allah nor denying the verse; he is free to want to use the way of striking, if he uses it correctly, or not to want to use it. For not all cases are the same, and marital problems differ in nature from house to house; so our Mighty Lord, Allah Most High, laid down a rule along which the relationship proceeds by degrees.

There remains the question of the nature of striking, because many men strike with a striking that harms, leaves a mark on the body, draws blood or breaks a bone, and this is something the Prophet ﷺ did not do. Yet it is important to establish that non-severe striking came linked to a specific, particular act, namely the wife bringing into the marital home a man from among her mahrams whom the husband dislikes and does not love. So it is a hadith that, in its explicit wording, did not address defiance (nushuz) in its generality and absoluteness; and nushuz in general means complete disobedience to the one in charge of the home. Whereas she who brings into her husband's house one of her mahrams whom her husband dislikes may do so out of defiance, or may do so without being defiant, for other reasons, among them emotion overcoming the wife and her wanting to make lunch in her home for her father, her brother, or her maternal uncle and his wife, while the husband is at odds with them all. So the hadith of non-severe striking came to address, in the explicit words of the hadith, the punishment of a specific, restricted act that may be defiance and may not be defiance. And in the understanding drawn from studying this hadith,""")

t(50, 60, """the man knows his wife and knows from living with her whether she brought into the house one of her mahrams whom he dislikes as disobedience to him, and so deserves the punishment, or because emotion overcame her, in which case gentleness and not striking her is preferable. He ﷺ said: (Your right over them is that they let no one you dislike tread your bedding. If they do that, strike them with a non-severe striking).

Linguistically, the definition of the word "mubarrih": it means severe, painful; so "non-mubarrih" means neither painful nor severe.

So is non-severe striking a punishment specified to be non-severe when the wife brings into the marital home a man from among her mahrams whom her husband dislikes? The answer is clear and the hadith is explicit.

Then we come to striking in the absolute sense, in the case of open disobedience and defiance that has no justification, while the wife is receiving her rights and yet disobeys. Here the noble verse comes in absolute terms, not specifying a particular act by designation as in the hadith. Here too we leave the sphere of the punishment for bringing into the house a man from among the mahrams whom the husband dislikes, whose punishment is non-severe striking! And we find a hadith narrated by Lady Aisha, Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her), about an incident between her and her husband the Prophet ﷺ! It is an incident in which the Prophet ﷺ punished her with a punishment that hurt her; that is, the blow was severe!

So the Prophet ﷺ did strike. Those who repeat the sentence "The Prophet never struck" are either ignorant people who do not read the hadiths, or liars with something in their hearts, perhaps under pressure from international bodies. In Muslim there is the saying of the Mother of the Believers Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): "Shall I not tell you about myself and about the Prophet ﷺ?" We said: "Yes." She said: "When it was my night, he ﷺ came back, placed his sandals by his feet, laid down his cloak and spread the edge of his lower garment on his bed. He waited only until he thought I had fallen asleep, then he put on his sandals slowly, took his cloak slowly, then opened the door and went out and closed it slowly. I put my shift over my head, then veiled myself with my lower garment and set out after him, until he came to al-Baqi. He raised his hands three times and stood for a long time, then he turned and I turned; he hastened and I hastened; he trotted and I trotted; he ran and I ran, and I got ahead of him and went in. I had only just lain down when he entered and said: (What is the matter with you, Aisha?) I said: Nothing. He said: (You will tell me, or the Subtle, the All-Aware will tell me.) I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, and I told him what had happened. He said: (So you were the dark shape I saw in front of me?) I said: Yes." She said: "Then he gave me a shove in the chest that hurt me"

Accordingly, Lady Aisha felt pain; that is, a severe blow fell on the rib cage.

Finally, the hadith "Do not strike the female servants of Allah" was said by the Prophet ﷺ before the revelation of the saying of Allah Most High: {As for those women whose defiance you fear, admonish them, leave them alone in their beds, and strike them. Then if they obey you, seek no way against them. Allah is Most High, Most Great}.

The upshot is that the Prophet ﷺ, out of a mercy on which he was created, ordered the Muslims in Madinah not to strike their wives, so the wives became defiant. Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet ﷺ and told the Prophet of the women's rebellion against their husbands in Madinah, so he ﷺ ordered a return to striking them. Thus the verse was legislation revealed after a back-and-forth that took place in the society of Madinah. And the upshot is that the verse {As for those women whose defiance you fear, admonish them, leave them alone in their beds, and strike them. Then if they obey you, seek no way against them. Allah is Most High, Most Great} was revealed to cancel and abrogate the hadith, which is the well-known hadith in the Sahih of al-Nasa'i, Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah. He said: "Do not strike the female servants of Allah." Then Umar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: "The women have grown bold against their husbands," so he permitted striking them. Then many women went round the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining of their husbands. So the Prophet ﷺ said: "Many women have gone round the family of Muhammad complaining of their husbands; those are not the best of you."

From all the foregoing we conclude the following:
🔴 Painful striking may happen, because we are human, and it occurred from the Prophet ﷺ
Painful striking does not mean flogging, crushing the body, breaking bones, or committing the disasters and calamities that Muslim husbands commit. Its upper limit is what happened to the Mother of the Believers Aisha
🔴 Painful striking must never be a method in striking, because the Prophet ﷺ did not do it as a habit and method; it occurred from him only once
🔴 Non-painful striking is that which causes slight pain, not harmful pain; it is a matter of judgement
🔴 Striking in itself the Prophet ﷺ did not practise as a habit or a method, whether the painful kind or the non-painful""")

t(51, 115, """Summary: in the relationship between spouses, as we see in the practice of the Prophet ﷺ, the basic rule is never, ever striking. But it is not said of one who struck his wife that he is not a man, nor is he to be insulted and transgressed against by a woman who does not understand her religion!""")

t(51, 600, """Slaves and children = human beings .. One of the most serious hadiths with an authentic chain, which millions of fathers and mothers do not know of because they take no care for their Hereafter .. Before mentioning the hadith ..

Our children whom we bring into the world are human beings, no less than the slaves who existed before the end of the age of enslaving human beings and holding them in bondage. If the Prophet ﷺ said a shattering word about the rights of enslaved slaves, then children, male and female, are no less than slaves in human right and in the right to obtain justice. A year ago a mother who has grown-up children and grandchildren consulted me. She asked me: "And will we be held to account on the Day of Resurrection for backbiting our children, since we backbite them morning and evening?" I said to her: "You will surely be held to account," and she went away unconvinced.

As for the rights of slaves, it is reported in the Sahih of al-Tirmidhi that a man sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: "O Messenger of Allah, I have two slaves who lie to me, betray me and disobey me, and I insult them and strike them. So how do I stand with regard to them?" He said: "Their betrayal of you, their disobedience and their lying to you will be reckoned against your punishment of them. If your punishment of them was equal to their sins, it will be even, nothing for you and nothing against you. If your punishment of them was less than their sins, it will be a surplus for you. And if your punishment of them was more than their sins, retribution for the excess will be taken from you for them." He said: The man moved aside and began to weep and cry out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: "Do you not read the Book of Allah: {And We set up the scales of justice for the Day of Resurrection, so no soul will be wronged in anything}, the verse." The man said: "By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I find nothing better for me and for them than parting from them. I call you to witness that they are all free."

This sensible man, a man of reason, understood; he grasped the truth and realised the enormity of the calamity .. So what a calamity for one who has backbitten his children morning and evening and harmed them for years and years and years, thinking they are possessions of flesh and blood with which he has the right to do as he pleases. That was a man who owned two slaves, and these are fathers and mothers who begot children and did not own them. The owner of slaves was not given the right to harm his slaves, so how about one who was born free, not owned?! Free sons and daughters .. Indeed, people on the Day of Resurrection are equal .. There is no difference between one who lived free and one who lived owned .. And people on the Day of Resurrection are, in their rights, like the teeth of a comb .. So let no father deceive himself .. and let no mother deceive herself .. O Allah, I have conveyed. O Allah, bear witness.""")

t(51, 2015, """Children visiting the abusive father .. Children visiting the abusive mother

Two years ago I spoke about a widely discussed issue and a recurring question: a man or a woman asks, because the problem exists with the son and the daughter alike. The question: "We are independent of our families, but we do not visit our father, because whenever we visit him he raises his hand against us, or insults and abuses us and hurts us, and we return to our homes weeping. Some of us have been afflicted with diabetes because of the harm of the father or the harm of the mother; some of us had our divorce caused by the father or the mother, and our children were lost and scattered; one of us, when he goes to visit his father, his father spits on him; one of us, when he goes to visit his father, his father abuses him with ugly words; and one of us, when he goes to visit his father, his father comes at him with a knife wanting to kill him." The cases are many. They ask: is stopping the visits in these cases permissible in the Shariah until Allah brings about a matter already decreed?

Answer: when the soul is exposed to destruction and the body is exposed to destruction because of the father or the mother, visiting lapses, because the preservation of life and of the mind are two of the five necessities that Islam has defined. Here contact remains""")

t(52, 60, """required only from afar, through correspondence. And if someone asks, and questions like these have in fact come to me before from more than one man and woman; if someone asks and says: "When I call, he absolutely does not answer my phone," or someone says: "I am living abroad, I am not a man of means, and my father or my mother has blocked me on WhatsApp, so how do I contact them?" And among people is he who barely has his day's food and the food of his dependants and cannot waste it on international calls. And among those who ask are some who say: "We call, but the father or the mother stays silent at the other end of the phone, not replying at all (gods on earth besides Allah)." The cases are many.

Summary: if your visiting your abusive father or your abusive mother is such that it has been established for you by experience, through the behaviour of a father or mother who gives no weight to reason or religion, that this visit means your being killed and your life taken, or your being exposed to harm that will afflict you with physical illnesses, because the harm is repeated at every visit and clear signs of illness appear in you, as those signs develop into a certain affliction with the diseases of grief, the best known of which is diabetes, which destroys a person's life and future; in these two cases, killing or being made ill, confirmed by proofs you see in yourself because of their harm, visiting ceases to be obligatory.""")

t(52, 1010, """((An educational counsellor)) says to people: everything said about a person carrying the crises of childhood with him into adolescence, then youth and the rest of his life, and about his being affected by harsh treatment in childhood, is empty talk, hollow talk, the talk of Western scholars far from Islam, and we do not have to follow the West in everything it says. ((The educational counsellor)) adds: the child's memory is weak and he forgets quickly; when he is subjected to harm he forgets quickly, as if nothing had happened. And gives a strange example, saying: "Do you not see children fight and then play with each other a few minutes later and forget everything?!"

This educational nonsense is an immoral licence for fathers and mothers who are mentally ill and of deviant nature to do every possible evil to their children. And I still say: by Allah, many of those who speak to people, if they knew the price of the word and the sentence they utter, and realised the gravity of speaking to people, and realised that on the Day of Resurrection they will be held to account for any corruption and ruin on earth, they would sew their mouths shut with a needle. But alas: self-admiration in one's opinion, and the temptation of speaking to the masses.""")

t(52, 1830, """Affection is given to the girl only!
The consultant answered: No .. Do not give your male son affection, so that he (turns out) a man
This is a destructive prescription for the child's soul. A woman calls a ((educational)) consultant and asks: "Should I give my male son affection as I give it to my daughter?" The question in itself is clear, easy and understandable, with no ambiguity in it that would call for the ((family consultant)) to scatter and branch off in misdirected directions! What calls for the ((family counsellor)) to say: "Do not give your son affection as you give it to your daughter, because that way your son will not (turn out a man)"?!!!!! Are there differences at all between affection for the boy and for the girl? What is the definition of affection for this ((family counsellor))? Does the definition of affection, for him, mean that the mother buys the boy a dress, for example?! Or puts an earring in his ear! The question was framed by the woman correctly and very clearly; by affection she means affection. But the one who answered the question laid down a new classification of affection and said: "The boy is not given affection like the girl!!" It is a strange answer, because the meaning of affection is hidden from no one, not even ordinary people who are not specialists. Affection is kisses, hugs, kind treatment and praise .. All of this is affection .. There is no mother who praises her male son in the same way she praises her female daughter, but in the end both acts are affection .. A mother hugging her male son is affection; has the hug become for females only? Where do they get these educational calamities, which they broadcast in educational lectures? The ((family counsellor)) here did not distinguish between terms, and considered the affection that the Prophet ﷺ gave to his grandsons …""")

t(53, 60, """… and to his son Ibrahim, peace be upon them all, and to Muslim children in general, male and female, and to his loved and beloved Zayd ibn Harithah, whom he treated with the highest of that affection, which the counsellor sees as a mistake that should not be given to males!! This counsellor, who always says "I speak by the Book and the Sunnah," says to the woman asking: "Encourage your son; say to him: you are a hero, you are a man, you are a lion; but do not give him affection!!!"

And this post is a correction for people so that they do not go astray, because the tear is wide, and whenever we come to patch it we at once find a new tear; and of those who speak it is always said: preachers!""")

t(53, 755, """There is no might and no power except with Allah. A mother calls a woman psychological counsellor and asks the counsellor: "Should I treat my male children with affection?" And the counsellor says to her: "No, do not treat the males with affection, so that they turn out men!"

Where is the affection of the Prophet ﷺ, overflowing and abundant, which was pampering and not mere affection, for al-Hasan and al-Husayn? Did al-Hasan and al-Husayn not turn out men? Is this guidance by the Book and the Sunnah?!!

With advice like this, criminal young men and selfish young men come out into society, because they never tasted affection, and their hearts grew up as dead hearts that know no mercy. O every male social counsellor .. O every female social counsellor .. Whoever is ignorant, let him sit at home .. whoever is ignorant, let his home suffice him .. Enough of destroying the Ummah with aberrant reasoning and thinking and with opposition to human nature, because of foolish personal opinions.""")

t(53, 1510, """Striking the wife in Islam has a method, a form, a manner and a way, and overstepping that is counted a clear violation in which there is no ambiguity and no dispute. And it is never accepted, nor lawful, nor permissible for a woman (a preacher) to come out and say to people: "Everyone who strikes his wife is not a man!" This is an explicit rejection of a clear, explicit verse in the Book of Allah Most High, and rejecting a verse in the Book of Allah Most High = disbelief. And we as Muslims will not see a verse in the Book of Allah rejected and applaud! Or say "No problem!" Or say "Never mind, we will not criticise, because this criticism will cut off the livelihood of the one we criticise!"

A brief word to any brother or sister on YouTube among the owners of channels that make a profit and who address millions of Muslims

Criticising the content of any channel on YouTube has nothing to do with cutting off livelihood! Unfortunately there is a very strange and odd confusion, and a misconception that celebrities fall into when they are criticised for what they present to people: they come out and say, "What have we done to you that you should cut off our livelihood!" O brothers, O sisters, owners of channels followed by millions: the reason for criticism is never the wish to cut off anyone's provision. This is an odd and strange confusion, unacceptable in logic and reason! Is it reasonable that I present worthless stuff to people and no one makes it clear to people, so that I can go on (earning my bread)? And who said that criticism cuts off a person's livelihood? How can a person present ideas to people and not know that his written provision will certainly come to him in the amount Allah Most High has written for him, whether someone criticises him or no one criticises him?! I do not understand how a person who presents ideas to people can miss this truth, which is clear to millions of Muslims, even those who never finished school.

Criticism takes place because what is presented is presented in public .. before everyone's eyes .. in front of hundreds of millions of listeners and viewers. This is not work carried out behind closed rooms, so that an error occurring in it is limited only to the visitors and clients; rather this is thought broadcast to people. So how can the error be seen and passed over in silence because of a mistaken method in people's minds whose title is: "Do not criticise what he says, for you will cut off his livelihood"? This is one of the strangest things that can be heard by a person who understands""")

t(54, 60, """Islam well and understands the meaning of the provision that Allah Most High sends to people. And this method, if it becomes general in people's minds, will be a calamity, because we will then leave the owners of pulpits to address people with anything and keep silent so that we do not cut off their provision?! Is this the talk of reason?

Summary: let no person, man or woman, fear for his provision on his channel. And let no man or woman who receives consultations fear because a criticism has fallen on the ideas they present. For provision, if it decreases, will not decrease because of criticism; rather it is written for it to decrease. And it is not permissible nor right for any channel owner to implant in the minds of Muslims this deviant idea about provision. For if he comes out and says, "You have struck at my provision because of your criticism of me," he implants in the minds of his followers a deviant understanding of destiny and of provision. And Allah is the One whose help is sought.""")

t(54, 825, """In the reactions that came to me regarding my post about Hala Samir yesterday, one must distinguish between criticism and refutation. The first reaction that came to me was a belief on the part of one of the brothers who follow me that I am refuting! I do not refute on my channel in general issues; I only clarify, and the difference between "refutation" and clarification is vast. The Majlis is not for refutations in general issues, because refutations in general issues are a method of "bench-gossip" and not a method of guidance. As for refutation, its basic meaning is a person refuting a per…""")

t(54, 1340, """170 or 195 countries without a visa .. The global political climate may determine the number .. My expectation, and Allah knows best, is that it will reach 195""")

t(55, 300, """A symbolic picture that does not express the real manner, but it is a symbol for the lesson .. a symbol for understanding .. a symbol for realisation .. A symbol for the awakening of many from the coma of illusion and the wrong ideas their minds have woven, because they understood nothing of the real, original story .. and only listened to the tales of legend .. He cries out among the people: "Will you allow him chicken once a week? Will you allow him three eggs for dinner? Is there anyone among you who does not eat? Is there among you …""")
